{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"18/10/2026 00:40:42","profile":{"player_id":"103926","last_updated":"18/10/2026 00:40","fullname":"Mahabalage Sineth Lakvan Mario Jayawardena","short_display_name":"S Jayawardena","name":"Sineth Jayawardena","gender":"M","dob":"25/12/2004","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"Sri Lanka","nationality_id":"8","nationality":"Sri Lanka","nationality_short_code":"SL","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"3","text":"All Rounder","role":"All Rounder"},"batting_style":{"id":"2","text":"Left Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"7","text":"Off break"},"writeup":"<p>Sineth Jayawardena is a left-handed batter who also bowls right-arm off-break. He came through Sri Lanka's youth pathway and featured prominently for the Under-19 side, eventually taking over the captaincy for the 2023 U19 Asia Cup in the UAE and leading Sri Lanka at the 2024 ICC U19 Cricket World Cup. He had already made his mark at youth level with a player-of-the-match 101 against Bangladesh U19 in a tri-series in the UAE.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nJayawardena made his senior debut for Panadura Sports Club in 2023, across First-Class, List A, and T20 formats, before moving to Tamil Union Cricket and Athletic Club. His List A career has included two centuries, with his highest score being a blistering 136 off 103 balls against Colombo Cricket Club, while he has also featured for Sri Lanka A, Sri Lanka Emerging, and Jaffna Kings in the Lanka Premier League.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nIn domestic T20 cricket, he has cemented his reputation as a destructive top-order option, highlighted by a rapid 101 off 52 balls against Panadura SC and a match-winning 82 off 32 balls in the final against SSC to lead Tamil Union to the 2026 title. Overall, he finished as the leading run-scorer in the Major Club T20 Tournament 2026, amassing 372 runs across 9 matches.</p>\r\n<p><br />\r\nHaving continued to develop through the domestic and Sri Lanka pathway setups, Jayawardena earned a place in Sri Lanka's 15-member squad for the 2026 Asian Games in Japan, where the side enters the men's T20 competition at the quarter-final stage.&nbsp;</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"8","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Sri Lanka"},{"id":"503","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Sri Lanka Emerging"},{"id":"718","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Panadura Sports Club"},{"id":"900","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Sri Lanka A"},{"id":"971","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Tamil Union Cricket and Athletic Club"},{"id":"1165","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"1","text":"Sri Lanka Under-19"},{"id":"2489","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Jaffna Kings"},{"id":"2759","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"SLC Greys"},{"id":"3894","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Cape Town Samp Army"}]},"international_debut":{"comp_type_id":"3","comp_type":"T20 International - m","match_id":"274308","match_center":"https://www.icc-cricket.com/matches/274308/india-vs-sri-lanka","series_id":"15773","series_name":"Asian Games Men’s T20I, 2026","match_date":"01/10/2026","for":{"id":"8","text":"Sri Lanka","short_name":"SL"},"vs":{"id":"4","text":"India","short_name":"IND"},"venue":{"id":"2703","text":"Korogi Sports Park, Nisshin"},"batting":{"runs":"","balls_faced":"2","hundreds":"0","innings":[{"number":"1","runs":"","balls_faced":"2","hundreds":""}]},"bowling":{"wickets":"","runs_given":"","ball_bowled":"","economy":"","five_wk_hauls":"0","innings":[]},"fielding":{"catches":"2","stumpings":"0","run_outs":"0","innings":[{"number":"1","catches":"2","stumpings":"0","run_outs":"0"}]}},"international_last_match":{"comp_type_id":"3","comp_type":"T20 International - m","match_id":"274139","match_center":"https://w